== Online Interaction Data

Each online policy-training episode combines one hydraulic base scenario from the training partition defined in @section:dataset:splits with a newly generated arsenic schedule. The policy determines the chlorine sequence as the simulation advances, and the simulator computes the network response defined in @section:dataset:simulation-setup. The resulting observations, actions, and network responses provide the interaction data for policy training.


== Training, Validation, and Test Data <section:dataset:splits>

The hydraulic base scenario is the indivisible split unit. Every prescribed chlorine profile, arsenic schedule, precomputed offline trajectory, online policy-training episode, and fixed control case inherits its scenario's assignment. Keeping each hydraulic realization within one partition prevents training and evaluation data from sharing demand, hydraulic, and chemical histories. The 100 base scenarios are divided into 80 training, ten validation, and ten test scenarios.

The precomputed offline trajectories are distributed across all three partitions. The training partition provides data for fitting forecasting models and scenarios for online policy training. Validation supports model development, while the test partition is reserved for final evaluation on unseen hydraulic realizations.

For control validation and testing, we generate separate collections of fixed arsenic schedules, referred to as catalogs, using the procedure described in @section:dataset:arsenic-events. These catalogs are separate from the schedule sets used for the offline dataset. Each validation or test scenario is combined with individual schedules to form fixed control cases. Validation scenarios are paired with five schedules each, while test scenarios are paired with ten. @tab:dataset-split summarizes the scenario allocation and the associated offline trajectories, online training use, and fixed control cases.

