== Reproducibility

All components of the dataset are generated deterministically. This includes the demand patterns, hydraulic parameter realizations, chlorine profiles, and arsenic schedules. Regenerating the dataset from the same configuration therefore reproduces the same hydraulic base scenarios, offline trajectories, and fixed control cases.

The offline dataset and control runs reuse the same hydraulic base scenarios and parameter realizations, but use separate seeds for their arsenic schedules. Each precomputed offline trajectory can be traced to its hydraulic base scenario, fixed arsenic schedule, and prescribed chlorine profile. The fixed control-validation and control-test schedules are likewise associated with their respective base scenarios. The seeds, generation procedures, and artifacts required for reproduction are documented in @section:appendix:dataset-artifacts.


== Dataset Summary

The hydraulic scenarios, arsenic schedules, and chlorine inputs together define the conditions under which the learning and control methods are studied. @tab:dataset-inventory summarizes these components in a compact overview of the network, temporal resolution, offline trajectories, and online interaction data.

The precomputed offline trajectories provide the data for forecasting and for generating #acr("MPC") teacher demonstrations for behavior cloning. The online interaction data comprise the observations, actions, and network responses generated during #acr("PPO") training. The next chapter explains how each data source is prepared for the respective models and incorporated into their training.

